parts[0].paragraphs.push("A course that compares tax-advantaged products should never make eligibility assumptions on a person's behalf. An account may be available to open even when the individual cannot make a deductible or otherwise qualifying contribution under the rules for that year. Before running any favorable tax projection, collect the account type, contribution year, compensation, filing information and stated use of the funds. Those inputs matter as much as the projected investment growth rate.");
parts[11].paragraphs.push("The concluding investment plan should be revisited at the beginning of each tax year and after changes to employment, health coverage or family needs. A worker who becomes eligible for an employer match may face a different contribution opportunity; someone buying a home may need more liquid savings; and a change in health plan can affect HSA eligibility. Continuing a contribution automatically does not mean it remains lawful or affordable. Review both eligibility and household cash before changing funding amounts.");
